Neither font is checked into this repository. Both are fetched from Google
Fonts at build time by next/font/google and self-hosted from this site's own
origin, so the deployed build redistributes the woff2 files and carries the
notice obligation in OFL section 2. That is why the two license texts above
are kept here rather than beside font files that do not exist in the source
tree.

The remaining dependencies are compiled into the build by Next.js. None of
them ships a NOTICE file requiring propagation under Apache License 2.0
section 4(d). Their licenses are declared in each package's own package.json;
bun.lock does not record license fields, so it is not the place to look.

Marks belonging to others are not bundled components and are not licensed to
this project. They appear on the site referentially, to identify the runtimes
Ensemblr drives and the platform it runs on: GITHUB and the INVERTOCAT logo
design (GitHub, Inc.), Claude and Claude Code (Anthropic, PBC), Apple, Mac and
macOS (Apple Inc.), and Pi (a project by Mario Zechner). The notice the site
prints in its footer is in src/lib/legal.ts.
